capability nats/events  connected, disconnected, reconnected, closed
  heroes  nats.is_closed, nats.stats_of, nats.take_errors
  go      ConnectHandler, DisconnectHandler, DisconnectErrHandler, ReconnectHandler, ReconnectErrHandler, ClosedHandler, Conn.SetClosedHandler, Conn.SetDisconnectHandler, Conn.SetDisconnectErrHandler, Conn.SetReconnectHandler, Conn.Status, Conn.StatusChanged, Conn.RemoveStatusListener, Status, Subscription.StatusChanged, SubStatus, Subscription.SetClosedHandler, NoCallbacksAfterClientClose
  rust    ConnectOptions::event_callback, Event, connection::State, Client::connection_state
  python  disconnected_cb, reconnected_cb, closed_cb, is_connecting
  note    a callback would need a closure; a program reads the state when its own loop asks, the reconnections counted and the client's end told by `is_closed`

