dropped
  go      Conn.Barrier (an order among callbacks, which do not exist here), Conn.Buffered (the bytes a buffered writer holds; every write here is written), Msg.Equal, Msg.Size, Status.String, SubStatus.String, Subscription.Type, Subscription.SetClosedHandler, WriteBufferSize, MultipathTCP, SkipHostLookup, IgnoreAuthErrorAbort, UserInfoHandler, Conn.IsSystemAccount, Conn.RemoteAccount, CustomDialer, ProxyPath (a proxy's path for a WebSocket; `websocket` dials no proxy), Conn.JetStream's options and every constant `Err*` (a failure here is a code of README § A4 and a message)
  rust    ConnectOptions::read_buffer_capacity, Client::try_server_info's option, every error kind enum (ClientError, ConnectErrorKind, client::FlushErrorKind, client::PublishErrorKind, client::RequestErrorKind, client::ServerPoolErrorKind, client::SetServerPoolErrorKind, client::SubscribeErrorKind, subject::SubjectError, CallbackError, UnsubscribeError, header::ParseHeaderNameError, header::ParseHeaderValueError, status::InvalidStatusCode), connection::ShouldFlush, Protocol, Server, datetime functions, traits Publisher, Requester, Subscriber, TimeoutProvider, IntoHeaderName, IntoHeaderValue
  python  CLOSED, CONNECTED, CONNECTING, DISCONNECTED, DRAINING_PUBS, DRAINING_SUBS, RECONNECTING (the state's names), msg_class, flusher_queue_size, pending_data_size, ssl_context, Subscription.pending_bytes's twin attributes, nuid, protocol, errors' classes (every one a code and a message here)
